-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Relationship to the Python implementation
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is a reimplementation in Rust of ALAS, previously written in Python with a
Wails desktop shell. The two share an author, a licence and a model catalogue;
they share no code. The Python implementation remains the reference against
which this one is validated, and the correspondence between them is recorded
module by module in docs/PORTING.md.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Network use
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Section 13 of the AGPL concerns making a modified version available to users
over a network. This program is a single desktop executable: it runs no server
and accepts no inbound connections. It makes outbound requests only when the
user asks it to -- fetching a flight plan, navigation data, or a map texture --
which does not engage section 13.

The Python implementation did run a loopback HTTP server, and its NOTICE
qualified this section accordingly. That qualification is no longer needed.


