-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This program contains code translated from other projects. A translation is a
derivative work: the original licence follows it into this tree, whatever
language it is written in. Two consequences are worth stating plainly, because
they are the ones a reader is most likely to question:

  * Modules translated from SUAVE (LGPL-2.1) carry that licence. LGPL-2.1
    section 3 permits a recipient to treat a copy under the ordinary GPL
    version 2 or any later version, which is compatible with AGPL-3.0, and this
    program relies on that route. Unlike the Python implementation -- which
    invoked SUAVE as a separate process and could argue it never combined with
    it -- this program links translated SUAVE code directly, so the combination
    rests on licence compatibility alone.

  * External solvers -- MSES, MSC Nastran, AVL, NASTRAN-95 -- are not
    distributed with this program and are not covered by this licence. They are
    separate executables, supplied and licensed by the user, which the program
    invokes if present. The program is fully functional without them, reporting
    the affected analyses as unavailable rather than substituting a silent
    approximation.

Every translated module names its origin, the upstream licence and the source
revision in a provenance header. THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md lists the components
one by one.
